@startuml architecture
title paddock: component architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor User

package "Herdr 0.8.0" {
  [Keybindings\nprefix+s -> the chooser\nprefix+shift+s -> the attach list\n(written by `paddock init`)] as Keybinding
  [herdr CLI\ntab create / pane run] as HerdrCLI
  [Workspace / tabs / panes] as HerdrUI
}

package "paddock" {
  [cli.py\nchoose | launch | attach | profiles | gc | logs | init\n~--cwd, ~--dry-run] as CLI
  [init.py\nsplice the keybinding into\n$HOME/.config/herdr/config.toml\n~--dry-run, ~--undo] as Init
  [tui.py\nthe chooser: fields, words and rules\nanswers -> a plan] as TUI
  [screen.py\nthe screens: form, list, checklist, box,\nconfirm, and the one a failed launch ends on\none prompt_toolkit Application each,\nplus the progress lines a slow launch prints] as Screen
  [recent.py\nthe profile each workspace\nlaunched last] as Recent
  [sessions.py\nsession registry\ncreate | attach | remove_pane] as Sessions
  [profiles.py\nProfile dataclass\nnetwork presets] as Profiles
  [agents.py\nagent registry\ncommand, domains, required tools,\ncredential paths,\nimage + install for the guest] as Agents
  [synth_config.py\nsynthesized config dir\n(credentials + ticked skills\n+ MCP whitelist)] as SynthConfig
  interface "Backend\nprepare(profile) -> run\nload_run(run_dir) -> run\nopen_pane(run, label)\n-> pane id\ncollect(run_dir)" as BackendAPI
  [sessions.BACKENDS\nbackend name -> the module\nthat runs it] as BackendRegistry
  [backends/srt.py\nbuild_settings / build_shim_dir\npane_command / prepare / open_pane] as SrtBackend
  [backends/__init__.py\nthe run dir both share:\nlaunch.json + launch.sh + pane.log\none launch script for both backends:\nstderr kept, and a failed launch held] as RunContract
  [backends/microsandbox.py\nmsb create / exec --tty / rm -f\nprepare / open_pane / collect\nboot script: install the agent, place\nthe token, copy the config in] as MsbBackend
  [herdr_client.py\ncreate_tab / run_in_pane\ncheck_config / reload_config\n(mockable seam)] as HerdrClient
  [log.py\nget_logger(__name__)\nfile at DEBUG, stderr at WARNING\n($PADDOCK_LOG, $PADDOCK_LOG_FILE)] as Log
}

package "Host configuration" {
  database "~/.config/paddock/\n(override: $PADDOCK_CONFIG_DIR)\nprofiles/*.json\nagents/*.json" as ConfigFiles
  database "~/.local/state/paddock/\n(override: $PADDOCK_STATE_DIR)\nruns/<id>/ launch.json + launch.sh + pane.log +\nwork/ (when the profile shares no dir),\nconfig/ for a redirected agent,\nplus for srt: bin/ + srt-settings.json\nsessions.json (registry: backend, vm_handle,\nrun_dir, pane ids per session)\nlogs/paddock.log (1 MB, 3 backups)\nworkspace default bindings (planned)" as RunDir
}

package "Sandbox runtimes" {
  [srt\nSeatbelt (macOS)\nbubblewrap (Linux)] as Srt
  [msb\nlibkrun microVM from an OCI image\nno daemon: one process per VM] as Msb
}

User --> CLI : runs `paddock init` once, after installing
CLI --> Init : init (backs the config up first)
Init --> Keybinding : writes the popup blocks\nand moves herdr settings to prefix+comma
Init --> HerdrClient : herdr config check, then reload-config\n(a refused config is put back;\nno herdr to ask is only a message)
User --> Keybinding : presses prefix+s
Keybinding --> CLI : popup runs `paddock`\n(HERDR_SOCKET_PATH,\nHERDR_ACTIVE_WORKSPACE_ID,\nHERDR_ACTIVE_PANE_ID)
CLI --> TUI : choose (default)
TUI --> CLI : one plan:\nlocal | attach | new session
TUI --> Screen : draws the form, one editor per field\nover it, the confirm, and what a launch\nis doing and why it failed
TUI --> Recent : which profile to open on
CLI --> Recent : remembers the profile a launch used
TUI --> Profiles : load / save profile
TUI --> Agents : list agents, remember a typed command
TUI --> Sessions : list live sessions
Sessions ..> RunDir : registry survives\nHerdr restart
Recent ..> RunDir : last-profile.json,\nper workspace
Profiles ..> ConfigFiles : reads / writes
Agents ..> ConfigFiles : reads user agents/*.json

CLI --> Sessions : launch_local | get_session + attach | launch\n(the only module that carries a plan out)
BackendAPI <|.. SrtBackend
BackendAPI <|.. MsbBackend

SrtBackend --> RunDir : writes PATH shim dir, srt-settings.json,\nconfig dir, scratch workdir, launch.json, launch.sh
MsbBackend --> RunDir : writes launch.json (vm_handle, workdir),\nlaunch.sh (`msb exec --tty <handle>`) and the\nconfig dir the guest mounts
SrtBackend ..> RunContract : launch.sh + pane.log + the pane line
MsbBackend ..> RunContract : launch.sh + pane.log + the pane line
Log ..> RunDir : appends logs/paddock.log
CLI ..> Log : `paddock logs` reads it back
Sessions --> BackendRegistry : backend_for(session.backend):\nprepare on create,\nload_run + open_pane on attach,\ncollect when the last pane goes
BackendRegistry --> SrtBackend : "srt"
BackendRegistry --> MsbBackend : "msb"
Sessions --> HerdrClient : launch_local: a plain tab,\nno session, no sandbox
SrtBackend ..> SynthConfig : build config dir
MsbBackend ..> SynthConfig : build(defer_credentials) + place_credentials,\nmounted read-only at /paddock-config-src and copied\nto /paddock-config in the guest (copies, not links)
Agents --> SynthConfig : credentials + whitelisted skills

SrtBackend --> HerdrClient : pane command + env
MsbBackend --> HerdrClient : pane command, and no env: the guest's\nvariables are set by `msb create -e`,\nwhich every later exec inherits
HerdrClient --> HerdrCLI : herdr tab create [~--workspace] ~--cwd ~--label\n[~--env KEY=VALUE ...] ~--focus\nherdr pane run <pane_id> `exec /bin/sh <run_dir>/launch.sh`\nherdr config check | herdr server reload-config
HerdrCLI --> HerdrUI : creates tab, returns\nresult.root_pane.pane_id
HerdrUI --> Srt : sandboxed pane process
HerdrUI --> Msb : `msb exec --tty` into the session VM,\nrunning the agent or the image's shell

note right of BackendAPI
  A backend works the whole launch out as
  plain functions, then opens the pane through
  herdr_client. That client is the seam every
  test mocks, so CI needs no herdr, no srt and no msb.

  Each session record names its backend.
  A name that is not in sessions.BACKENDS
  fails at attach with a message; the
  registry still loads.
end note

note bottom of HerdrClient
  The only module that shells out to `herdr`.
  Mocked in every test; CI has no herdr server.
end note

note bottom of Log
  Every module logs through this one, under its own
  name, so `paddock.backends.srt` says which layer
  wrote the line. Never a token, a credential file's
  contents, an environment value, a proxy URL or a
  traceback: paths, byte counts and lengths instead.
  `paddock logs` prints the path and the last 40 lines.
  A run's pane.log is the agent's own output and carries
  no such promise, which `paddock logs <session>` says.
end note

note right of Sessions
  The one door. cli.py and tui.py never import a
  backend, and no backend imports them or sessions.py.
  tests/test_architecture.py parses the imports and
  fails on any edge that breaks that (SPEC section 10).
end note

@enduml
